# 19. BLOCKED USER BEHAVIOR

Implement blocking securely on the backend.

Do NOT rely only on frontend JavaScript.

The server/database must verify:

* Sender is authenticated.
* Recipient exists.
* Sender has not blocked recipient.
* Recipient has not blocked sender.
* Conversation belongs to the requesting user.
* User has permission to perform the requested action.

A malicious user must not be able to bypass blocking by directly calling an API endpoint.

