# 28. SECURITY

This is extremely important.

Implement backend authorization.

Never trust:

* User IDs from frontend.
* Conversation IDs.
* Message IDs.
* Block status sent by client.
* Delete permissions sent by client.

Every request must be verified server-side.

Users must only be able to access conversations they are participants in.

Users must not be able to:

* Read another user's private conversations.
* Delete another user's messages.
* Modify another user's account.
* Impersonate another user.
* Change another user's chat ID.
* Bypass blocking.

Sanitize message content appropriately.

Prevent:

* XSS
* Injection attacks
* Unauthorized API access
* ID enumeration where practical
* Duplicate message creation
* Spam abuse

Rate-limit message sending and user-search endpoints where appropriate.

